update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'<p>Decision: Figure plausible and sourced? If not, flag it.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Past reports</p>\n<p>Out: ME-F07 records</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: By end of 2027</p>\n<p>Control: Each figure carries its source</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Record new events</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Enter each new event from the final SitRep, DROMIC and RDANA; update after the PDNA.</p>\n<p>Decision: Aggregate counts only?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Final SitRep; DROMIC; RDANA; PDNA</p>\n<p>Out: ME-F07 record</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 30 days of the final SitRep</p>\n<p>Control: Version history kept</p>\n<p>Escalate: EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Check quality</th>\n<th>Second person in Research and Planning</th>\n<th><p>Check totals against sources and flag inconsistencies.</p>\n<p>Decision: Consistent?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Records</p>\n<p>Out: Quality log</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Each January and July</p>\n<p>Control: Flags resolved or noted</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Use and share</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Produce summaries for the annual report, the CDRA update and Sendai monitoring.</p>\n<p>Decision: Summary needs small-count review? Ask the DPO.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Database</p>\n<p>Out: Summaries</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Each January</p>\n<p>Control: DPO review where needed</p>\n<p>Escalate: DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Database standard; ME-F07 records with sources; quality log; summaries.\n\n### SOP 7-08 \\| Lessons, Peer Learning and Manual Revision\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Research and Planning, with the Manual custodian. **Purpose:** Turn lessons from the City''s own events and from other LGUs and networks into documented changes, including new versions of this Manual.\n\n**Table 7.28**\n\n**SOP 7-08 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                                                                 |\n|-----------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP7-08 (proposed); MODE Library versions                                                                    |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | CDRRMO Head approves Manual versions; CDRRMC or the Mayor for changes needing an issuance                                 |\n| Process owner (operational) | M&E unit; Manual custodian                                                                                                |\n| Trigger                     | An approved AAR or IAT result; a peer exchange or network event; a change in law; the annual lessons review each February |\n| Forms                       | ME-F08; ME-F05                                                                                                            |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A10.9 (2, Low); A10.6 (2, Medium)                                                                                         |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-11; MR-18; MR-01                                                                                                       |\n| Policy basis                | UNDRR Scorecard 6.6.1; MCR2030; RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)                                                                       |\n| Cross-references            | All chapters; Chapter 8 (networks); Chapter 1 (document control)                                                          |\n\n**Table 7.29**\n\n**SOP 7-08 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Capture</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Record each lesson with its source and the change proposed.</p>\n<p>Decision: Is a change proposed? If not, it is an observation, not yet a lesson.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: AAR; IAT; exchange report</p>\n<p>Out: ME-F08 entry</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 15 days of the source</p>\n<p>Control: Source linked</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Record peer exchanges</th>\n<th>Participant</th>\n<th><p>After an exchange or network event, record what was learned and its relevance to Ormoc.</p>\n<p>Decision: Relevant to a gap or a procedure?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Event materials</p>\n<p>Out: ME-F08 entry</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 10 days</p>\n<p>Control: Change proposed or "none"</p>\n<p>Escalate: M&amp;E unit</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Decide</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Decide whether to change a plan, form, procedure, training or MODE rule; open a CAPA entry if so.</p>\n<p>Decision: Change within CDRRMO authority? If not, refer to the CDRRMC.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: ME-F08</p>\n<p>Out: Decision; ME-F05 entry</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Monthly</p>\n<p>Control: Decision recorded</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Revise the Manual</th>\n<th>Manual custodian</th>\n<th><p>Draft the change as a new version in the Library; update the revision record and traceability links.</p>\n<p>Decision: Does the change alter authority or legal readings? Then the City Legal Office reviews.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Decision</p>\n<p>Out: Draft version</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 30 days of the decision</p>\n<p>Control: Approved versions are never edited</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Legal Office</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Approve and communicate</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Approve the version; brief affected staff and offices.</p>\n<p>Decision: Approved?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Draft version</p>\n<p>Out: Approved version; briefing record</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On approval</p>\n<p>Control: Only the CDRRMO Head approves</p>\n<p>Escalate: —</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Review annually</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>In February, review the lessons register: lessons with no change, changes with no effect.</p>\n<p>Decision: Patterns found?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: ME-F08; ME-F05</p>\n<p>Out: Annual lessons review</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: February</p>\n<p>Control: Presented to the CDRRMC</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** ME-F08 lessons register; decisions; CAPA entries; Manual versions and revision records; briefing records; annual lessons review.\n\n### SOP 7-09 \\| Protection of DRRM Data: Notices, Sharing and Breach Response\n**Process owner:** City Data Protection Officer, with the CDRRMO privacy compliance officer. **Purpose:** Handle personal data in DRRM lawfully and securely, and respond to breaches as the NPC requires.\n\n**Table 7.30**\n\n**SOP 7-09 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                                          |\n|-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP7-09 (proposed)                                                                    |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | City Mayor as personal information controller acting through the DPO; NPC for breach notifications |\n| Process owner (operational) | City DPO; CDRRMO privacy compliance officer                                                        |\n| Trigger                     | New form or data flow; new data-sharing need; annual review; a suspected breach                    |\n| Forms                       | ME-F09                                                                                             |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A5.5 (2, Medium)                                                                                   |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-15; MR-10; MR-07                                                                                |\n| Policy basis                | RA 10173 and IRR; NPC Circular No. 16-03; NPC Circular No. 2023-06                                 |\n| Cross-references            | Section 12; Chapters 4 and 5 (registration and relief forms); Chapter 6 (distribution records)     |\n\n**Table 7.31**\n\n**SOP 7-09 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Map the data</th>\n<th>Privacy compliance officer</th>\n<th><p>List DRRM forms and systems that hold personal data, with purpose, office and retention.</p>\n<p>Decision: Is each item necessary for its purpose?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Forms; systems</p>\n<p>Out: Data inventory (ME-F09 part A)</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Annually</p>\n<p>Control: DPO reviews</p>\n<p>Escalate: DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Notify</th>\n<th>Owning office with DPO</th>\n<th><p>Add privacy notices to registration, evacuation and relief forms.</p>\n<p>Decision: Notice states purpose, sharing and retention?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Forms</p>\n<p>Out: Revised forms</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before the typhoon season</p>\n<p>Control: DPO approves the text</p>\n<p>Escalate: DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Secure</th>\n<th>City ICT office; platform custodian</th>\n<th><p>Apply role-based access, logging and encryption; review access lists.</p>\n<p>Decision: Access limited to need?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Access lists</p>\n<p>Out: Access review record</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Quarterly</p>\n<p>Control: NPC Circular No. 2023-06 measures</p>\n<p>Escalate: DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Agree sharing</th>\n<th>City Legal Office with DPO</th>\n<th><p>Sign data-sharing agreements with offices and partners that exchange personal data with the CDRRMO.</p>\n<p>Decision: Agreement in place before sharing?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Sharing needs</p>\n<p>Out: Signed agreements (ME-F09 part B)</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before sharing</p>\n<p>Control: Register of agreements</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Administrator</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Contain a breach</th>\n<th>Office that finds it; DPO</th>\n<th><p>Report a suspected breach to the DPO at once; contain it.</p>\n<p>Decision: Personal data affected?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Incident</p>\n<p>Out: Breach log (ME-F09 part C)</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Immediately</p>\n<p>Control: Time of knowledge recorded</p>\n<p>Escalate: DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Assess and notify</th>\n<th>DPO</th>\n<th><p>Assess risk; where notification is required, notify the NPC and affected data subjects.</p>\n<p>Decision: Notification required under NPC Circular No. 16-03?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Breach log</p>\n<p>Out: Notifications</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 72 hours of knowledge</p>\n<p>Control: Copy of notifications kept</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Learn</th>\n<th>DPO with M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Record causes and corrective actions in the CAPA register.</p>\n<p>Decision: Action identified?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Breach log</p>\n<p>Out: ME-F05 entry</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 15 days</p>\n<p>Control: Closed only when effective</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Data inventory; revised forms; access reviews; data-sharing agreements; breach log; notifications; CAPA entries.\n\n## 15. Responsibility Assignment (RACI)\n\n| **\\[R\\] Responsible** | **\\[A\\] Accountable** | **\\[C\\] Consulted** | **\\[I\\] Informed** |\n|-----------------------|-----------------------|---------------------|--------------------|\n\n"A" is the single proposed process-accountable owner; "R" performs; "C" is consulted; "I" is informed. The RACI allocates work; it does not transfer legal powers.\n\n**Table 7.32**\n\n*RACI for Monitoring, Evaluation and Learning*\n\n| **Activity**                           | **CC** | **MY** | **HD** | **ME** | **TWG** | **EOC** | **AS** | **VA** | **DPO** | **ACC** |\n|----------------------------------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------|---------|--------|--------|---------|---------|\n| LDRRMP indicator set and annual report | A      | I      | R      | R      | R       | I       | –      | –      | C       | C       |\n| IAT fieldwork and scoring              | I      | –      | A      | R      | C       | C       | R      | –      | C       | –       |\n| IAT validation and release             | I      | –      | A      | R      | C       | C       | C      | R      | –       | –       |\n| After-action review                    | I      | I      | A      | R      | C       | R       | –      | –      | –       | –       |\n| CAPA register                          | C      | I      | A      | R      | R       | R       | –      | –      | –       | C       |\n| 45-day post-declaration report         | I      | A      | R      | R      | C       | R       | –      | –      | –       | R       |\n| Event and loss database                | I      | –      | A      | R      | C       | C       | –      | –      | C       | –       |\n| Lessons and Manual revision            | C      | I      | A      | R      | C       | C       | –      | –      | –       | –       |\n| Data protection and breach response    | I      | A      | R      | C      | I       | C       | –      | –      | R       | –       |\n\n*Note. CC = CDRRMC; MY = City Mayor; HD = CDRRMO Head; ME = M&E unit (CDRRMO Research and Planning); TWG = CDRRMP Technical Working Group focal offices; EOC = EOC Manager and staff; AS = assessors; VA = validators; DPO = City Data Protection Officer; ACC = City Accountant. For data protection, the Mayor is accountable as head of the personal information controller, acting through the DPO.*\n\n## 16. Performance Monitoring, Quality Assurance and Corrective Action\n\nThis chapter measures itself with the same discipline it applies to others.\n\n**Table 7.33**\n\n*Performance Measures for Chapter 7*\n\n| **Measure**                                                         | **Evidence**                      | **Review Owner**  |\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|-------------------|\n| Annual LDRRMP results report presented in January                   | ME-F02; CDRRMC resolution         | CDRRMC            |\n| Share of LDRRMP indicators with a baseline and current value        | ME-F01                            | CDRRMO Head       |\n| IAT cycle completed and validated on schedule; no self-validation   | MODE cycle record; validation log | CDRRMO Head       |\n| Share of triggers with an approved AAR within the set timing        | AAR register; ME-F03, ME-F04      | CDRRMO Head       |\n| CAPA items overdue; items closed as effective; recurring findings   | ME-F05                            | CDRRMC, quarterly |\n| 45-day reports submitted by day 45                                  | GOV-F13; submission proof         | CDRRMC; OCD VIII  |\n| Mandated reports submitted on time                                  | ME-F06                            | CDRRMO Head       |\n| Events in the database with sourced figures                         | ME-F07; quality log               | CDRRMO Head       |\n| Lessons with a documented change                                    | ME-F08                            | CDRRMO Head       |\n| Data-sharing agreements in place; breaches notified within 72 hours | ME-F09                            | DPO               |\n\n## 17. Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities\n\n**Table 7.34**\n\n*Implementation Priorities for Chapter 7*\n\n| **No.** | **Action**                                                                                                                                                     | **Office**                                 | **IAT**      | **When**                                         |\n|---------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|--------------|--------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Prepare the 45-day report template (Annex 7-D, GOV-F13) and confirm the reporting route with OCD VIII.                                                         | CDRRMO Head                                | A10.8        | Before the workshop                              |\n| 2       | Hold the validation workshop under SOP 7-03; re-score the FGD-only items with evidence first.                                                                  | CDRRMO Head; M&E unit                      | All          | 1–4 December 2026                                |\n| 3       | Designate the M&E unit and the AAR facilitators by office order.                                                                                               | CDRRMO Head                                | A10.4, A10.6 | December 2026                                    |\n| 4       | Produce the first annual LDRRMP results report (ME-F02) with the ME-F01 matrix and baseline.                                                                   | M&E unit; TWG focal offices                | A10.4        | January 2027                                     |\n| 5       | Open the CAPA register (ME-F05) and load the IAT High and Medium gaps.                                                                                         | M&E unit                                   | MR-14        | December 2026                                    |\n| 6       | Attach existing AAR reports and the plan revisions they produced, for validation.                                                                              | CDRRMO                                     | A10.6, B7.4  | Before the workshop                              |\n| 7       | Confirm the DPO designation; sign data-sharing agreements with CSWDO and CPDO; add privacy notices.                                                            | City Administrator; DPO; City Legal Office | A5.5         | First quarter 2027                               |\n| 8       | Adopt the event and loss database standard and back-load events from 1991.                                                                                     | M&E unit                                   | A5.4         | Standard by March 2027; back-load by end of 2027 |\n| 9       | Record changes adopted from MCR2030, NRC and Project TRANSFORM exchanges.                                                                                      | M&E unit                                   | A10.9        | Next annual lessons review                       |\n| 10      | Platform: add root cause, verification and effectiveness fields to actions (or a CAPA table); add event and loss tables; load templates for SOPs 7-01 to 7-09. | Platform data custodian                    | MR-11, MR-14 | Before the first annual report                   |\n\nValidation: each SOP is reviewed by the offices named in its control block, the AAR procedure is tested in the first exercise after adoption, and the data-protection procedure is reviewed by the DPO and the City Legal Office before adoption.\n\n## 18. Forms, Registers and Annexes\n\n**Table 7.35**\n\n*Chapter 7 Forms and Registers*\n\n| **Code** | **Form or Register**                                                | **Used in**          | **MODE**                             |\n|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------|--------------------------------------|\n| ME-F01   | LDRRMP M&E matrix (aligned with Form 5D of the 10-Year Plan)        | SOP 7-01             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F02   | Annual LDRRMP progress and results report                           | SOP 7-01             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F03   | After-action review report (full and focused forms)                 | SOP 7-04             | Proposed; receives ER-F06            |\n| ME-F04   | Exercise evaluation report (full and short forms)                   | SOP 7-04             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F05   | Corrective and preventive action (CAPA) register entry              | SOPs 7-03 to 7-09    | Proposed; MODE actions for IAT items |\n| ME-F06   | Reporting calendar and compliance tracker                           | Section 10; SOP 7-06 | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F07   | Disaster event and loss record                                      | SOP 7-07             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F08   | Lessons and peer-learning register entry                            | SOP 7-08             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F09   | DRRM data inventory, sharing register and breach log (parts A to C) | SOP 7-09             | Proposed                             |\n| GOV-F13  | Post-lifting 45-day report (Chapter 1, Annex 1-G)                   | SOP 7-06             | Seeded                               |\n| ER-F06   | After-action and corrective action record (Chapter 4)               | SOPs 7-04, 7-05      | Seeded                               |\n\nAnnexes: **7-A** IAT and master requirements traceability; **7-B** LDRRMP M&E matrix template; **7-C** after-action review report outline; **7-D** 45-day post-declaration report outline; **7-E** disaster event and loss database fields.\n\n## 19. Relationship With Other Chapters\n\n**Table 7.36**\n\n*Links Between Chapter 7 and the Other Chapters*\n\n| **Ch.** | **Title**                                                                 | **Link**                                                                                                                                         |\n|---------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Legal Mandate, DRRM Governance and Institutional Accountability           | Defines the CAPA register, governance KPIs and records management that this chapter operates; GOV-05 and PR-LIFT-REPORT start the 45-day report. |\n| 2       | CDRRMO Organisational Structure, Staffing and HR Management               | Staffs the M&E unit; receives AAR findings on staffing and rosters.                                                                              |\n| 3       | Risk Intelligence, Planning and Institutional Preparedness                | Owns the LDRRMP and CDRA that this chapter monitors; receives the event and loss database for risk assessment.                                   |\n| 4       | Early Warning, EOC Activation, Incident Management and Emergency Response | Sends the hot wash, ER-F06 and SitReps; receives AAR findings.                                                                                   |\n| 5       | Recovery, Rehabilitation and Build Back Better                            | Sends recovery monitoring and closeout lessons; receives PDNA data back through the database.                                                    |\n| 6       | DRRM Financing, Resource Management and Accountability                    | Sends utilisation reports and COA findings; receives corrective actions on funds, stocks and inventory.                                          |\n| 8       | Stakeholder Engagement and Institutional Partnerships                     | Manages the networks whose exchanges this chapter records.                                                                                       |\n| 9       | Public Awareness, Community Resilience and Capacity Development           | Runs the exercise programme that this chapter evaluates; delivers training actions from the CAPA register.                                       |\n| 10      | Institutional Sustainability, Deep Resilience and Recognition             | Uses IAT results, AARs and the CAPA record as evidence for recognition systems and the improvement agenda.                                       |\n\n## 20. Concluding Notes\n\nThe City has the pieces of a learning system: a results-based M&E design in its 10-Year Plan, a Council with the duty to monitor, a working group with thematic focal offices, regular reports to OCD and the DILG, and now a full institutional baseline. What it lacks is the loop that ties them together: one register, one calendar, one database, and the habit of closing an action only when it has worked.\n\nWriting these procedures does not implement them. Until the first annual results report has been presented, the first validated IAT cycle has fed the CAPA register, one event or exercise has gone through an AAR to verified closure, and the 45-day report template has been agreed with OCD VIII, this chapter remains a controlled working draft.\n\n## References\n\nThe official text governs.\n\nArgyris, C., & Schön, D. A. (1978). *Organisational learning: A theory of action perspective*. Addison-Wesley.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2023). *Ormoc City disaster risk reduction and management ten-year plan (2023–2032)*.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026a). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC institutional assessment tool* (Version 1.7) \\[Unpublished assessment workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026b). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC master requirements traceability and 140-indicator data dictionary* (Version 1.2) \\[Unpublished project reference workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026c). *MODE architecture decision records ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-014 and ADR-029* \\[Repository documents, version 1.16.0\\]. https://github.com/asilvainnovations/ormoc-drrmo\n\nCity Government of Ormoc, Office of the City Mayor. (2022–2024). *Executive Order Nos. 2022-00020, 2023-0026 and 2024-032A*.\n\nDepartment of the Interior and Local Government Region VIII. (2025). *Adoption of the harmonised disaster response reporting template and SOP* (Memorandum R08-LGCDD-2025-02-26-008).\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2017). *Memorandum No. 147, s. 2017*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2018). *Memorandum No. 131, s. 2018: Guidelines on the establishment, operationalisation and management of the emergency operations center*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2020). *National disaster risk reduction and management plan 2020–2030* and its results-based monitoring and evaluation plan.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2022). *LDRRMP formulation guidebook*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2026). *Implementing rules and regulations of Republic Act No. 12287* (signed 14 September 2026).\n\nNational Privacy Commission. (2016). *Circular No. 16-03: Personal data breach management*.\n\nNational Privacy Commission. (2023). *Circular No. 2023-06: Security of personal data in the government and the private sector*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 9470. (2007). *National Archives of the Philippines Act of 2007*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10121. (2010). *Philippine Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Act of 2010*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10173. (2012). *Data Privacy Act of 2012*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 12287. (2025). *Declaration of State of Imminent Disaster Act*.\n\nUnited Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2015). *Sendai framework for disaster risk reduction 2015–2030*.\n\nUnited Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2017). *Disaster resilience scorecard for cities: Detailed level assessment*.\n\n## Annex 7-A. IAT and Master Requirements Traceability\n\n**Table 7.37**\n\n*IAT Rows, Master Requirements and Chapter 7 Procedures*\n\n| **IAT** | **Type** | **Weight (W)** | **Score** | **Gap Priority** | **Master Requirements**              | **SOP**           | **Recommended Action (IAT v1.7)**                                                                                                                           |\n|---------|----------|----------------|-----------|------------------|--------------------------------------|-------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| A10.3   | M        | 2              | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-02; MR-07; MR-01; MR-12–15        | Section 10        | Adopt RDRRMC VIII Res. No. 12-006 locally by CDRRMC resolution; confirm the harmonised template is used.                                                    |\n| A10.4   | M        | 2              | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-07; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-01              | Produce the first annual RBME report (Form 5D) and baseline database; present it to the CDRRMC and LDC; include IAT results and CDRA monitoring indicators. |\n| A10.6   | GP       | 2              | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-07; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-04, 7-05        | Validate AAR reports and the plan revisions they produced.                                                                                                  |\n| A10.8   | M        | 2              | 0         | 12.0 High        | MR-07; MR-11; MR-16; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 7-06              | Prepare the 45-day post-declaration report template and confirm the route with OCD VIII.                                                                    |\n| A10.9   | GP       | 1              | 2         | 2.0 Low          | MR-11; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-08              | Document changes adopted from exchanges.                                                                                                                    |\n| A5.4    | GP       | 2              | 0         | 8.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-07; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-07              | Set up a disaster event and loss database (Sendai and DesInventar fields) and back-load past RDANA and PDNA data.                                           |\n| A5.5    | M        | 2              | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-07; MR-10; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 7-09              | Confirm the City DPO; sign data-sharing agreements with CSWDO and CPDO; add privacy notices to registration forms.                                          |\n| B7.3    | M        | 2              | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-04; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-04 (evaluation) | Run an annual exercise programme testing EOC activation (Chapter 9); evaluate each exercise here.                                                           |\n| B7.4    | GP       | 2              | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-04; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-04, 7-05        | Track AAR actions in an improvement plan.                                                                                                                   |\n\n*Note. Copied from IAT v1.7 and the Traceability and Data Dictionary v1.2. Scores and priorities are for validation (Methodology v1.1, section 6). SOPs 7-02 and 7-03 serve all 140 indicators and MR-12 to MR-15.*\n\n## Annex 7-B. LDRRMP M&E Matrix Template\n\nOne row per indicator. Aligned with Form 5D of the Ormoc City DRRM 10-Year Plan and the M&E matrix of the NDRRMP 2020–2030 RBME Plan.\n\n**Table 7.38**\n\n*M&E Matrix Columns (ME-F01)*\n\n| **Column**               | **Content**                                                               |\n|--------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Code and result level    | Unique code; impact, outcome, output or input and process                 |\n| Indicator and definition | What is counted, how, and what is excluded                                |\n| Unit and disaggregation  | Unit; sex, age, disability and barangay where relevant                    |\n| Baseline                 | Value and year, with source                                               |\n| Targets                  | By year to 2032, as approved by the CDRRMC                                |\n| Data source and method   | Office records, surveys, SitReps, IAT, database                           |\n| Frequency                | Quarterly, annual or per event                                            |\n| Responsible office       | Thematic focal office and data provider                                   |\n| Framework codes          | Ten Essentials; NDRRMP outcome; DILG pillar; Sendai target; IAT indicator |\n| Current value and status | Value, date, on-track or off-track, explanation                           |\n\n## Annex 7-C. After-Action Review Report Outline\n\n**Table 7.39**\n\n*Contents of an AAR Report (ME-F03)*\n\n| **No.** | **Section**                 | **Content**                                                                                |\n|---------|-----------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Event and scope             | Event or exercise, dates, hazard, area, EOC level, declarations; what the AAR covers       |\n| 2       | Method and participants     | Facilitator; offices and positions taking part; sources used                               |\n| 3       | Timeline                    | Official warning products with IDs; decisions; activations; key SitReps; resource requests |\n| 4       | What was supposed to happen | Plans, SOPs and protocols that applied                                                     |\n| 5       | What happened               | Facts, with evidence                                                                       |\n| 6       | What worked                 | Practices to keep, with evidence                                                           |\n| 7       | What did not work and why   | Findings with root or contributing causes; single- or double-loop                          |\n| 8       | Actions                     | Recommended actions with owner, due date and resources, entered in the CAPA register       |\n| 9       | Inclusion and protection    | How women, children, older persons and persons with disabilities were reached; gaps        |\n| 10      | Approval                    | CDRRMO Head approval; items referred to the CDRRMC                                         |\n\n*Note. Records name positions, not individuals. Personal data of affected people is not included.*\n\n## Annex 7-D. Post-Declaration (45-Day) Report Outline\n\nBasis: RA 12287 IRR Rule VI Sec. 1. The required content (declaration status, AA fund utilisation, estimated economic and social costs minimised) is followed; the remaining sections are proposed to make the report usable for learning. The outline will be revised when the NDRRMC issues the AA monitoring and evaluation framework.\n\n**Table 7.40**\n\n*Contents of the 45-Day Report*\n\n| **No.** | **Section**                         | **Content**                                                                                                                     | **Basis**                     |\n|---------|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|\n| 1       | Declaration status                  | Hazard; area; PDRA; CDRRMC recommendation; RDRRMC VIII action; Mayor''s EO; dates of declaration and lifting; ground for lifting | Rule VI Sec. 1                |\n| 2       | Anticipatory actions                | Measures carried out by lead office and barangay; people and assets covered (aggregate)                                         | Proposed                      |\n| 3       | AA fund utilisation                 | Spending by source and measure; tranche compliance; unused funds transferred to the STF                                         | Rule VI Sec. 1; Rule V Sec. 3 |\n| 4       | Economic and social costs minimised | Estimate with method and assumptions                                                                                            | Rule VI Sec. 1                |\n| 5       | Lessons                             | Summary of the AAR findings and actions                                                                                         | Proposed                      |\n| 6       | Annexes                             | EO; lifting record (GOV-F12); FIN-F06 closure                                                                                   | Proposed                      |\n\n## Annex 7-E. Disaster Event and Loss Database Fields\n\n**Table 7.41**\n\n*Minimum Fields of the Event and Loss Record (ME-F07)*\n\n| **Field Group**                      | **Fields**                                                                                                                                     | **Sendai Link** |\n|--------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------|\n| Event                                | Event ID; name; hazard type; start and end dates; source agency product IDs; declarations in force                                             | —               |\n| Location                             | Barangays affected (PSGC codes); area description                                                                                              | —               |\n| Human effects                        | Dead; missing; injured; affected persons and families; displaced in and outside evacuation centres (aggregate, by sex and age where available) | A, B            |\n| Housing                              | Houses partially and totally damaged                                                                                                           | B, C            |\n| Economic loss                        | Direct loss by sector (agriculture, infrastructure, housing, business), PHP, with valuation method                                             | C               |\n| Critical infrastructure and services | Damaged health and education facilities, roads, bridges, power and water; duration of service disruption                                       | D               |\n| Response and AA                      | Whether an EOC activation, State of Calamity or State of Imminent Disaster applied; AA carried out                                             | G               |\n| Sources and quality                  | Source document for each figure; date; quality flag; reviewer                                                                                  | —               |\n\n*Note. Aggregate counts only. Blank means "not reported". Small counts are reviewed by the DPO before publication.*\n\n## Validation and Source Control Register\n\n**Table 7.42**\n\n*Validation and Source Control Register*\n\n| **Item**                         | **Source Used**                                                      | **Status**                                                    |\n|----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|\n| IAT rows and scores              | IAT v1.7 workbook in the repository (12 Nov 2026)                    | Pending validation, 1–4 December 2026                         |\n| M&E design and reporting outputs | Ormoc City DRRM 10-Year Plan 2023–2032, Chapter 5 and Table 33       | Confirm Form 5D and reporting dates with the CPDO             |\n| RA 10121 Sec. 12(c) item numbers | Cited in IAT v1.7 (A5.4, A10.4)                                      | Check item numbers against the official text                  |\n| 45-day report content            | RA 12287 IRR Rule VI Sec. 1; GOV-F13                                 | Route to be confirmed with OCD VIII; AA M&E framework pending |\n| Local EOs on M&E                 | EO 2022-00020; EO 2023-0026; EO 2024-032A, as summarised in IAT v1.7 | Attach copies in the Vault                                    |\n| NPC circulars                    | NPC Circulars No. 16-03 and No. 2023-06                              | DPO to confirm current text                                   |\n| Validation controls              | ADR-029 (MODE v1.15.0)                                               | Proposed; for the CDRRMO Head to accept before the workshop   |\n| AAR and exercise timings         | Proposed by this chapter                                             | For CDRRMC adoption                                           |\n\n**CHAPTER 8**\n'
